.TH SDL_AtomicDecRef 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_AtomicDecRef \- Decrement an atomic variable used as a reference count.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_atomic.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_AtomicDecRef(a)    (SDL_AddAtomicInt(a, -1) == 1)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR "Note: If you don\(aqt know what this macro is for, you shouldn\(aqt use it!"

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I a
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_AtomicInt
to decrement\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the variable reached zero after decrementing, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

